195:### 4.3 What `applyPass` checks
197:`applyPass` (`src/framework/passes/define-pass.ts:190`) runs a pass and publishes nothing unless every stage succeeds: it freezes and hashes the result, diffs the two projections, refuses writes outside the declaration (`undeclaredWrite`), checks the contract the caller supplies (`contractRejected`), and checks each preservation claim (`preserveViolated`). `Program.apply` (`program.ts:248`) always supplies the **optimization contract** (`optimizationContract`, `passes.ts:221`), whose single condition is the invariant `typed.meaning-kept` (`meaningKept`, `evaluate.ts:564`).
199:### 4.4 The meaning contract
201:`typed.meaning-kept` generates cases (a function, arguments and an initial memory image) from r0, runs r0 and the candidate on each with the evaluator `evaluate` (`evaluate.ts:345`), and compares the outcomes with `agrees` (`evaluate.ts:531`): a trap agrees with any trap; otherwise the results and the memory written must be equal. By default it uses 40 cases per function, seed 7, and a step limit of 20,000 statements; a case that hits the limit on either side is *inconclusive* and decides nothing.
